  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find $r$ for which\n$$\\frac{1+r+r^2+r^3+\\cdots}{1-r+r^2-r^3+\\cdots}=2.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$r=\\frac13$.",
      "worked": "Both series converge when $|r|<1$. Their first terms are $1$ and their common ratios are $r$ and $-r$, respectively.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1+r+r^2+r^3+\\cdots}{1-r+r^2-r^3+\\cdots}&=\\frac{\\frac{1}{1-r}}{\\frac{1}{1+r}}\\\\\n\\frac{1+r+r^2+r^3+\\cdots}{1-r+r^2-r^3+\\cdots}&=\\frac{1+r}{1-r}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1+r}{1-r}&=2\\\\\n1+r&=2(1-r)\\\\\n1+r&=2-2r\\\\\n3r&=1\\\\\nr&=\\frac13.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\left|\\frac13\\right|<1$, both sums converge and this value is valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
